Description: settings and onboarding for Myna dictation
 Myna Settings is the desktop application that sets up and configures Myna,
 the local speech-to-text dictation service shipped as the myna snap. It
 guides installing the myna snap and a speech backend snap from the store,
 connects them, binds the dictation shortcut, and exposes the dictation
 settings (streaming mode, language, HUD style) that the daemon reads live.
 .
 It runs unconfined on the host because it drives snapd and runs snap
 commands as root through polkit, which a confined snap cannot do. The
 GSettings schema the daemon and this application share is installed by this
 package.
 .
 It also ships the Myna Dictation Indicator GNOME Shell extension, which
 shows dictation status as a focus-safe overlay, and for Xfce a small
 session service that shows the same indicator while dictation is running.
